    "short_description": "Lidl France is a discount supermarket chain that has been operating since 1989, offering a variety of affordable groceries and household essentials. It is part of the international Lidl group, which originated in Germany. The first Lidl store in France opened in Sarreguemines, marking the company's expansion beyond Germany. Over the years, Lidl France has grown significantly, reaching 1,000 supermarkets by 2002 and introducing various product innovations.\n\nThe store features a wide range of products, including private-label items, national brands, bakery sections, and fair-trade products under the Fairglobe brand. Lidl France is committed to sustainability, focusing on waste reduction and responsible sourcing. The company has implemented initiatives to cut food losses and organic waste by 50% by 2030 and supports sustainable practices in its supply chain. With logistics platforms established in Illkirch and Noisseville, Lidl France continues to serve individual retail consumers with everyday low prices.",
